# File: .nojekyll
#
# PURPOSE
#   Tells GitHub Pages to publish this repository exactly as it is, without
#   running it through Jekyll.
#
# WHY IT MATTERS HERE
#   1. Jekyll ignores directories whose names begin with an underscore. Keeping
#      Jekyll out of the way means no path in this project can ever disappear
#      because of that rule.
#   2. It removes any chance of Jekyll transforming or reformatting the single
#      file build (Password-Strength-Analyzer-standalone.html) or the generated
#      browser data files in frontend/js/data/.
#   3. It makes deployments faster, because no site is generated at all.
#
# GitHub Pages treats the mere presence of this file as the switch; its contents
# are ignored. The comment above is for the reader.
